===============================================================================
Upstream: easyPARM
===============================================================================

metalparm-vwf packages the easyPARM force-field parameterization pipeline as
visual workflow nodes. The scientific pipeline scripts bundled under each EasyParm
node's scripts/ directory are redistributed from easyPARM:

    easyPARM - Automated, Versatile, and Reliable Force Field Parameterization
    Workflow for Metal-Containing Molecules with Unique Labeling of
    Coordinating Atoms.
    Abdelazim M. A. Abdelgawwad and Antonio Frances-Monerris.
    Institut de Ciencia Molecular (ICMol), Universitat de Valencia.
    J. Chem. Theory Comput. 2025, 21, 4, 1817-1830.
    https://github.com/abenmb/easyPARM

    Copyright 2024 Abdelazim M. A. Abdelgawwad, Universitat de Valencia.
    Distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1.

The bundled easyPARM scripts retain their original copyright and license
headers unchanged. Node integration is handled by separate wrapper modules
(node.py / core.py), so the scientific scripts are redistributed as-is.

===============================================================================
Original work (metal-md authors), also under LGPL-2.1
===============================================================================

The following are original to metal-md and contain no easyPARM code:

  - All node wrappers: */node.py, */core.py, */meta.toml
  - snp_builder, peptide_builder, fragment_align
  - ep_fragment_fuse_topology, ep_apply_coords
  - ep_charges, xtb_opt, ep_amber_to_gromacs
  - md_solvate_packmol, md_solvate_gmx, md_membrane_build
  - md_traj_center, md_analysis_helix, md_analysis_distance

A small number of assembly / cleanup helpers (e.g. the no-ULS pass-through
variants of easyPARM steps, and metal_nonbon_fill.py) are original
reimplementations informed by the easyPARM pipeline; each acknowledges that
lineage in its module docstring.

